Hardening Container Image

Before hardening

FROM ubuntu:
RUN apt-get update
RUN apt-get -y install curl
ENV URL https://google.com/this-will-fail?secret-token=
CMD ["sh", "-c", "curl --head $URL=2e064aad-3a90-4cde-ad86-16fad1f8943e "]

After hardening 

FROM ubuntu:20.04                                                                     # Specific version
RUN apt-get update && apt-get -y install curl                        # update and install command should run together to prevent update layer caching issue
ENV URL https://google.com/this-will-fail?secret-token=     
RUN rm /usr/bin/bash                                                                # remove bash binaries to ensure noone can access bash in this container
CMD ["sh", "-c", "curl --head $URL$TOKEN"]                          # Remove hardcoded tokens, instead use variable 


podman build -t app .
podman run -d -e TOKEN=2e064aad-3a90-4cde-ad86-16fad1f8943e app sleep 1d # run in background
podman exec -it 4a848daec2e2 bash # fails
podman exec -it 4a848daec2e2 sh # works


Now by-default this container will run as root,  harden the container image to use appuser instead of ROOT


FROM ubuntu:20.04
RUN apt-get update && apt-get -y install curl
ENV URL https://google.com/this-will-fail?secret-token= 
RUN rm /usr/bin/bash
RUN adduser -D -g '' appuser                                                         # create app user 
USER appuser                                                                                      # USER can be set to app user
CMD ["sh", "-c", "curl --head $URL$TOKEN"]


